{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/vfs/Cargo.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:46:35.581129Z","id":"f11bf9fefc4c1c7045c250523e959afa17d15b757f332271f3988991d6b66673","body":{"detail":"vfs/Cargo.toml:12 says unsafe is allowed in exactly one function, file_name; crates/clax-worker/vfs/src/lib.rs:396 also allows it on xFileControl (SQLiteVfsFile::from_file and VfsStore::app_data). Both uses are sound given rsqlite-vfs's invariants: the name pointer lives from xOpen to xClose, SQLite passes the handle xOpen filled (szOsFile is size_of::<SQLiteVfsFile>()), and pAppData is the VfsAppData register_vfs leaked. AGENTS.md (Code) says \"No unsafe: the workspace lints forbid it\"; clax-worker is excluded from the workspace (Cargo.toml:11:12), so the forbid lint does not reach it and it sets deny with allows instead.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":9},"end":{"line":14},"content_hash":"866faa1b998a11d7ca227291938f56d345c4b8cb03a34adce2610e62cf48b4ce"},"suggested_fix":"Fix the comment to name both functions; the owner decides whether the exception stands or the file name is kept in the Rust file type to avoid file.name().","summary":"The crate allows unsafe in two functions, not the one its manifest comment names, and is an exception to AGENTS.md's no-unsafe rule that needs the owner's call","tags":["unsafe","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/vfs/Cargo.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:24:31.783907Z","id":"8996884f4238bce79170f7dd18ff21da20124188e4ed6de7605a376acc549952","body":{"detail":"As of git:0bf47593, crates/clax-worker/vfs/Cargo.toml:9:13 names file_name and IoMethods::xFileControl. xFileControl's unsafe now also reads SQLITE_FCNTL_PRAGMA's argument array and writes the refusal message it allocates with sqlite3_malloc (crates/clax-worker/vfs/src/lib.rs:558:613); no function was added to the exception. The 'no unsafe code' gate in scripts/quality_gates.sh (lane_lint: find crates -name '*.rs' -not -path '*/target/*') scans crates/clax-worker too and fails on this branch, at crates/clax-worker/vfs/src/lib.rs:428, 559, 570, 585 and 601, so scripts/quality_gates.sh cannot pass until the exception is decided: either the gate excludes this file, or the unsafe goes.","kind":"comment","references":"f11bf9fefc4c1c7045c250523e959afa17d15b757f332271f3988991d6b66673","summary":"The manifest comment now names both functions; the no-unsafe-code gate fails on this crate","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/vfs/Cargo.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:15:09.084429Z","id":"480dead379722429abffb870ea942316784194e8fb997f246cb3f78291d2ab69","body":{"detail":"0.2.0 (the latest release as of 2026-10-13) makes register_vfs an unsafe fn and keeps SQLiteVfsFile::name unsafe, so using it would bring unsafe back into the crate, which forbids it. 0.1.1 is pinned exactly because Registry::handles (crates/clax-worker/vfs/src/lib.rs:430:442) relies on 0.1.1's xOpen passing add_file the same String buffer it then leaks into the handle; a version that changes this makes every handle lookup fail with SQLITE_IOERR (every VFS test fails), not reach a wrong file, as long as the leaked buffer is the one add_file saw.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":18},"end":{"line":21},"content_hash":"3458f63c8404f79e6f905b2e17caf93cc35cf6a02c0a7757f7029c1cf11332dd"},"summary":"Upgrade rsqlite-vfs to 0.2.0","tags":["dependencies","revisit:a release of rsqlite-vfs registers a VFS and names a handle's file through safe functions","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/vfs/Cargo.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:24:21.807798Z","id":"c45efb39221d004b9fc507035f940d14073a76ed1f88caae0bc8cdf8e8aa1f91","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f8fa8f75","summary":"The owner decided: \"No unsafe in our code.\" Fixed: crates/clax-worker/vfs has no unsafe code and forbids it (#![forbid(unsafe_code)] in src/lib.rs, unsafe_code = \"forbid\" in Cargo.toml). file_name's unsafe SQLiteVfsFile::name() is replaced by Registry::handles, keyed by the name buffer's address that add_file is passed and the handle keeps; the xFileControl override is gone: the commit boundary is xSync, a post-commit truncation is stored when SQLite makes it, and the connection's authorizer refuses journal_mode, locking_mode and synchronous=OFF. Evidence: the 'no unsafe code' lane of scripts/quality_gates.sh run alone exits 0; cd crates/clax-worker && cargo test -q --workspace passes (adversarial 14, vfs 5, worker 33); cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -D warnings, native and wasm32 (lib targets), pass; node test-wasm.mjs ok; node e2e.mjs ok (19 checks).","supersedes":"f11bf9fefc4c1c7045c250523e959afa17d15b757f332271f3988991d6b66673","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
